# Copy to .env and fill in your values
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
JWT_SECRET=change-this-to-a-random-string
CORS_ORIGINS=http://localhost:5173,http://localhost:3000
RATE_LIMIT_MAX=100
RATE_LIMIT_WINDOW=60
# Declares this host a development environment. Every boot guard keys off it:
# the default JWT secret, DEMO_MODE, encryption-at-rest and the DATABASE_URL
# fallback below are ALL refused unless this says dev/local/test/ci. Unset means
# production — that is deliberate, so forgetting it on a deploy costs you a
# startup error rather than a silently disabled protection. Never set it on a
# real deploy.
ARCEO_ENV=dev
# Postgres. Unset = the docker-compose dev default (postgres/postgres@localhost/arceo),
# and that fallback now requires ARCEO_ENV above to name a dev environment.
# Production deploys MUST set DATABASE_URL explicitly.
#
# ⚠️ Note this file is NOT auto-loaded — export these, or use `docker compose`.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://postgres:postgres@localhost:5432/arceo
# Trust X-Forwarded-For for rate-limit keys. Leave OFF unless this app sits
# behind an ingress YOU control. When ON, ARCEO_TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS is REQUIRED
# and the app refuses to start without it — there is no safe default:
#   0 = the client IP is the RIGHT-MOST X-Forwarded-For entry (direct Cloud Run)
#   1 = second from the right (a Google Cloud Load Balancer in front of it)
# Too low and a caller can forge their own rate-limit bucket; too high and every
# caller collapses into one and the 11th login from anyone is refused.
# TRUSTED_PROXY=
# ARCEO_TRUSTED_PROXY_HOPS=
#
# ⚠️ Do NOT set FORWARDED_ALLOW_IPS=* (the common Cloud Run recipe). uvicorn's
# ProxyHeadersMiddleware would then rewrite the peer address from the left-most,
# caller-written X-Forwarded-For entry BEFORE the app sees it, re-creating the
# spoof above even with TRUSTED_PROXY off. The Dockerfile pins the flag to
# loopback so the env var cannot take effect there.
# Per-org ceiling on the CODE EXTRACTION endpoints (Tier 2.6). These are billed
# to ARCEO, not the caller: one /extract-github request is up to max_files (25)
# Haiku calls at max_tokens=8000. Keyed per org rather than per IP, because the
# cost lands on us per tenant and an IP key lets one customer's CI rotate around
# it. Deliberately tighter than RATE_LIMIT_LLM_MAX — the units are not comparable.
RATE_LIMIT_EXTRACT_MAX=20
RATE_LIMIT_EXTRACT_WINDOW=60
# Default monthly cap applied to an org that has set none. Still 0 = no cap.
# ⚠️ Turning this on is step (3) of Tier 2.6 and is BLOCKED: MED-015-b needs
# email-verification infrastructure that does not exist, so a non-zero default
# would lock out legitimate new signups. Steps (1) metering and (2) the
# extraction limiter above have shipped; a cap could never have tripped before
# them, because Arceo's own spend moved no counter at all.
# ARCEO_DEFAULT_MONTHLY_BUDGET_USD=0
# LLM-classification cache (a local SQLite file, deliberately separate from the
# app DB). Default: backend/llm_cache.db
ARCEO_LLM_CACHE_PATH=
